&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pelago is the leading specialty substance use care provider, built on the belief that effective treatment means matching care intensity to what each member actually needs rather than defaulting to the most expensive intervention. Our programs guide members through every stage of the substance use spectrum, from unhealthy habits to active use disorders, delivering personalized treatment for tobacco, alcohol, opioid, cannabis, and stimulant use based on individual health, habits, genetics, and goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With Sona, our voice-first AI Mental Health Specialist, Pelago now applies that same clinically-driven model to mental health, pairing deep clinical expertise with technology to expand access without compromising care quality. We believe technology should make clinical care more precise and more human, not replace the judgment behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pelago has scaled to helping hundreds of employers and health plans and has already helped more than 750,000 members better manage their substance use. If you&#39;re passionate about AI and making an impact on the health of others, join us and make it happen!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pelago is seeking a mission-driven, board-certified Addiction Medicine Physician with deep expertise in Substance Use Disorder (SUD) treatment to join our clinical team.&lt;/strong&gt; In this role, you&#39;ll provide direct member care via telehealth, delivering evidence-based SUD treatment to help individuals overcome addiction and achieve lasting recovery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to make a meaningful impact in digital SUD care delivery, working with cutting-edge telemedicine technology to reach members who need specialized psychiatric support. You&#39;ll be part of a collaborative, interdisciplinary team dedicated to transforming addiction treatment through innovative, accessible care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote and part-time role, averaging approximately 10 hours per week, open to candidates located in the United States&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;IMLC is strongly preferred.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide comprehensive SUD care to Pelago members via virtual visits, including thorough assessments, diagnosis, and medication management for SUD and co-occurring conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prescribe and monitor Medication Assisted Treatment (MAT), including naltrexone, Suboxone, and other evidence-based pharmacotherapies, in close collaboration with our member operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address concurrent mental health issues, such as mild to moderate anxiety, depression, sleep disorders, and other conditions frequently found with SUD, in collaboration with the clinical team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within Atlas, Pelago&#39;s AI-native EHR, which automates session documentation, surfaces real-time evidence-based guidance during calls, and prepares clinical context before each session — so your time stays focused on member care, not administrative lift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with counselors, coaches, and member operations to deliver optimized, coordinated care that enhances the member experience and supports recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to clinical excellence through participation in case reviews, journal clubs, grand rounds, and peer reviews to maintain high-quality, evidence-based care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop personalized treatment plans and offer referrals based on clinical assessments and individual member needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate and up-to-date clinical documentation, supporting quality assurance and compliance efforts to ensure the best patient outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate patients in a way that is tailored to their unique needs, abilities, and recovery goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on cross-functional projects with counselor, growth, and product teams to improve care delivery and member outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help refine and implement clinical protocols, treatment standards, and policies to enhance overall care quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commit to 10 hours per week supporting our patients.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The background we are looking for…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Board-certified physician (MD or DO) in one of the following:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Psychiatry (ABPN or AOA), with significant SUD treatment experience; Addiction Psychiatry subspecialty preferred, or&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Medicine, Family Medicine, or other ABMS/AOA primary specialty, with Addiction Medicine subspecialty certification (ABPM) or board eligibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Active licensure in at least one U.S. state&lt;/strong&gt;; multi-state licensure strongly preferred. Must be willing to obtain additional state licensure as needed (Pelago will sponsor this).
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;OK or PA preferred to support current patient demand&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;DEA registration (or in process) and current state-controlled substance license (or in process).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Comfort working in an AI-augmented care environment; openness to adopting AI-assisted tools that support documentation, member communication, and clinical decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Experience in telemedicine, with advanced comfort level using digital platforms and electronic health records (EHRs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;A passion for patient-centered care, innovation in addiction medicine, and continuous quality improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across teams and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMLC (Interstate Medical Licensure Compact) participation&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in digital health or telemedicine environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; At this time, we are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this position. There may be a 5-10% travel requirement in states requiring in-person assessments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The provided range reflects our US target hourly range for this part-time or contract position. Individual pay within the range will vary based on a variety of factors like role-related experience and education, internal pay equity, and other relevant business factors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pelago is the leading specialty substance use care provider, built on the belief that effective treatment means matching care intensity to what each member actually needs rather than defaulting to the most expensive intervention. Our programs guide members through every stage of the substance use spectrum, from unhealthy habits to active use disorders, delivering personalized treatment for tobacco, alcohol, opioid, cannabis, and stimulant use based on individual health, habits, genetics, and goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With Sona, our voice-first AI Mental Health Specialist, Pelago now applies that same clinically-driven model to mental health, pairing deep clinical expertise with technology to expand access without compromising care quality. We believe technology should make clinical care more precise and more human, not replace the judgment behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pelago has scaled to helping hundreds of employers and health plans and has already helped more than 750,000 members better manage their substance use. If you&#39;re passionate about AI and making an impact on the health of others, join us and make it happen!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Pelago Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our engineering team operates as empowered, outcome-oriented problem solvers, working in close partnership with product, design, and clinical teams to improve member outcomes at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As AI transforms how software is built, we are intentionally evolving our development lifecycle so we spend less time on mechanical implementation and more time on system design, judgment, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outcome-driven: Engineers are given problems to solve, not just features to build. Success is measured by learning, impact, and outcomes—not velocity alone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native: We use AI across the SDLC to accelerate implementation, testing, and review. Engineers focus on defining intent, validating behavior, and designing resilient systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy, high accountability: Teams have real ownership over their domains. With autonomy comes responsibility for quality, safety, and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional by default: Engineers partner deeply with Product, Design, Data, and Clinical. Discovery, experimentation, and delivery are shared responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality and safety matter: We build in a regulated, member-impacting domain. Reliability, observability, and correctness are first-class concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Instead of task lists, anchor on ownership:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own meaningful problem spaces end-to-end, from discovery through delivery and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve systems that support safe, scalable, AI-augmented development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and experimentation to validate whether solutions actually work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally to balance member impact, clinical constraints, and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how we work—our tools, processes, and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;We explicitly assess for empowerment:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You start with &quot;why&quot; before diving into &quot;how&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by ambiguity and collaborative problem-shaping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI to amplify your judgment and move faster on what matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in systems and anticipate second-order effects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to own outcomes, not just ship features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of the Role: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Pelago is building behavioral health care delivery from the ground up – AI-native, outcome-oriented, and built for a domain where what you ship has direct consequences for member health. Product Engineers own meaningful problems end-to-end: from discovery through production and iteration, in close partnership with product, design, data, and clinical stakeholders. The hire we&#39;re looking for is technically strong enough to ship across the stack, fluent enough with AI tooling to move fast, and grounded enough to make sound trade-offs in an environment where member safety, privacy, and reliability matter as much as speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role with a high-collaboration rhythm (3 days/week in our NYC office).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own meaningful product areas end-to-end — from problem framing and prototype through production rollout and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with product, design, data, and clinical teams to shape solutions that improve member outcomes and business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve secure, well-tested, observable software across backend, frontend, and data surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, experimentation, and user feedback to validate whether shipped solutions are working, and drive iteration when they&#39;re not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate autonomously in ambiguous environments, communicating proactively across globally distributed teams and functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound trade-offs across speed, safety, technical quality, and maintainability in a regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve Pelago&#39;s engineering system: AI-native development practices, testing, documentation, knowledge sharing, and review quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Background We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong production experience building product software in a startup or scale-up environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent TypeScript/Node capability; comfortable working across APIs, services, data and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense:&amp;nbsp; able to start from the user or business problem, not just the implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating autonomously in ambiguous environments and making sound trade-offs with incomplete information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid testing, observability, and reliability instincts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent with AI-augmented engineering workflows while maintaining human judgment and QA discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, digital health, or safety-sensitive regulated software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event-driven systems, serverless AWS, relational database design, and infrastructure as code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with experimentation, analytics, and growth/product instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to both backend and user-facing product surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products from 0 to 1 in an early-stage environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At this time, we are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note that Pelago is dedicated to providing accommodations to candidates upon request. If you need accommodations at any point throughout the interview process, please reach out to your recruiter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
